# @glue/math_silicon — the Mesland correspondence between math-altitude
# mathematical structures and silicon-altitude executable realizations.
# The first @glue species after the family-root landing at `8d3f89e`;
# the LOAD-BEARING species for the Cholesky arc's first empirical
# crystal.
#
# === The recognition (Cholesky arc closure, 2026-07-01) ===
#
# Per `docs/specs/reality-algebra-math-and-glue.md` §2.1 + §3.3.1 the
# math ↔ silicon Mesland correspondence carries LAPACK-class discharges
# (Cholesky decomposition + triangular solve as the first empirical
# case) + the Chamseddine-Connes spectral action numerical machinery
# (the #74 candidate operationalizes here). This shard is the
# substrate-decl form of the correspondence at species altitude,
# forward-promised at `shards/glue.mirror` §"Forward-promised
# inheritors" and at `shards/reality/algebra/math.mirror` §
# "Forward-promised inheritors" and at
# `shards/reality/algebra/silicon.mirror` §"Composition with siblings
# via @glue".
#
# The Cholesky arc composes four shards end-to-end:
#
#   1. `shards/epistemologic/math/cholesky.mirror` — the theorem shard
#      (predicate: symmetric-positive-definite ⇒ LL^T decomposition).
#   2. THIS SHARD — @glue/math_silicon
#      The Mesland correspondence carrying the LAPACK realization as
#      morphism_kind; the composition mechanism between math (#1) and
#      silicon (#3).
#   3. `shards/reality/algebra/silicon.mirror` (Mara `9ca6723`, LANDED)
#      — the silicon species; the target altitude.
#   4. LAPACK dpotrf / dpotrs FFI binding — Reed's discharge boundary.
#
# This shard is the COMPOSITION MECHANISM. It carries the typed
# correspondence surface + the discharge machinery + the bilateral
# with @fate for selection. It does NOT re-declare Tomm probes (per
# Taut Pass-2 discipline); the morphism-category discipline is
# inherited via `in @glue`.
#
# === The correspondence shape ===
#
# Per `shards/glue.mirror` §"The correspondence carrier" the Mesland
# correspondence record carries (source_prism, target_prism,
# morphism_kind, restriction). For math ↔ silicon:
#
#   source_prism:   @reality/algebra/math
#   target_prism:   @reality/algebra/silicon
#   morphism_kind:  @arxiv/math/cholesky_decomposition.lapack_realization
#                   (initial); OPEN enumeration extending to
#                   @arxiv/math/eigendecomposition.lapack_realization,
#                   @arxiv/math/svd.lapack_realization,
#                   @arxiv/math/lu_factorization.lapack_realization,
#                   @arxiv/math/qr_factorization.lapack_realization,
#                   @arxiv/math/spectral_action.chamseddine_connes_
#                   numerical, ...  per @fate tournament expansion.
#   restriction:    precision:    { f32, f64, complex64, complex128 }
#                   conditioning: well-conditioned
#                                 (κ(A) ≤ 1/√ε for the field's ε)
#                   layout:       column-major (LAPACK's native ABI)
#
# The restriction is what @fate's dice rolls MUST land within; @fate
# cannot select a morphism outside these bounds (per
# `shards/fate.mirror` §"The dice roll constraints" — γ + J symmetry
# preservation composes on top).
#
# === Uses @fate for selection ===
#
# @glue/math_silicon does NOT compute the LAPACK discharge directly.
# Per `shards/glue.mirror` §"The load-bearing action" the composition
# is:
#
#   @glue × @fate → typed translation outcome
#
# When `translate(c_math_silicon, math_payload)` fires:
#
#   1. c_math_silicon carries the (math, silicon, morphism_kind,
#      restriction) tuple.
#   2. @glue invokes @fate.roll(restriction, hole) where hole is
#      derived from (math_payload, silicon_signature, silicon_
#      altitude).
#   3. @fate's dice roll selects one morphism's OID within the
#      restriction — e.g., dpotrf vs zpotrf vs LDL^T variant — the
#      constrained-inference operator picks based on the payload's
#      (field, dimension, conditioning-hint).
#   4. @glue applies the selected morphism to the math payload; the
#      selected realization's FFI body computes the silicon-altitude
#      output.
#   5. The translation_outcome IS the composed
#      lower_triangular_matrix + LAPACK info-parameter + residual
#      opacity wrapped in
#      imperfect<lower_triangular_matrix, ref, transparency(
#      correspondence)>; the crystal lands in the @bauchladen tray
#      under `@fate/algebra/morphism/math_silicon` per
#      `bauchladen-autopoietic-fate.md` §5.
#
# The bilateral is HARD: the translate action's body MUST invoke
# @fate.roll (not a direct deterministic compute). This is the
# discipline that distinguishes @glue/math_silicon from a bare FFI
# wrapper — the LAPACK routine to use is @fate-selected within the
# restriction, and each selection accumulates as a Bauchladen crystal
# the next cycle's tournament browses.
#
# === Non-reflexive counterpart to @reality/algebra/math ===
#
# Per `shards/reality/algebra/math.mirror` §"Connes A side":
# `@reality/algebra/math` is the HIGHEST-REFLEXIVE species (A IS the
# content). Per `shards/reality/algebra/silicon.mirror` §"Connes A side":
# `@reality/algebra/silicon` is the NON-REFLEXIVE counterpart (A acts
# UPON silicon-altitude carriers).
#
# The @glue/math_silicon correspondence lifts one side into the other:
# math's reflexive-A becomes, under translation, silicon's A-acting-
# upon-transistor-states. The morphism_kind ref names the specific
# lift (Cholesky's LL^T decomposition as a math-altitude theorem
# lifts to LAPACK's dpotrf as a silicon-altitude executable
# realization). The restriction bounds the lift's admissible instances
# (precision, conditioning, layout).
#
# The @glue.compose composition IS non-commutative here: composing
# c_math_silicon with c_silicon_math (the reverse; forward-promised)
# does NOT return the identity correspondence. Reason: dpotrf followed
# by symbolic reconstruction loses precision on non-representable
# entries; the composition's transparency carrier surfaces the
# residual opacity per the [ω, ω] cross-term (per `shards/glue.mirror`
# §"The categorical composition").
#
# === Bilateral obligations from @glue ===
#
# @glue/math_silicon MUST discharge the three obligations @glue's
# family-root declares:
#
#   - `morphism_well_typed(c_math_silicon)` — every morphism the
#     correspondence admits must have source_signature in
#     `@reality/algebra/math`'s H_math and target_signature in
#     `@reality/algebra/silicon`'s H_silicon; the discharge is via
#     the restriction's typing on precision/conditioning/layout.
#   - `translation_uses_fate(translate_math_silicon)` — the
#     species' translate body invokes @fate.roll on every call
#     (not a direct deterministic compute); the substrate-pull-
#     honest discipline preserved at species altitude.
#   - `restriction_preserved(c_math_silicon, payload)` — the
#     math payload's field + dimension + conditioning-hint must
#     be within the restriction's typed bound.
#
# The three obligations conjointly imply `glue_witnessing(c)` at the
# species altitude; consumers add `requires glue_witnessing(c)` when
# they pull @glue/math_silicon.
#
# === Forward-promised morphism kinds ===
#
# The species' morphism_kind enumeration is OPEN; each morphism_kind
# addition is a per-consumer pull. Initial kinds:
#
#   @arxiv/math/cholesky_decomposition.lapack_realization
#     Cholesky's LL^T decomposition; the FIRST empirical crystal
#     for the arc; LAPACK dpotrf (real) / zpotrf (complex); Reed's
#     FFI binding operationalizes here.
#
# Forward-promised additions (per §3.3.1 open enumeration):
#
#   @arxiv/math/eigendecomposition.lapack_realization
#     A = QΛQ^{-1}; LAPACK dsyev / zheev; the substrate's
#     `sheaf_laplacian.lambda_zero` action already discharges here.
#   @arxiv/math/svd.lapack_realization
#     A = UΣV^*; LAPACK dgesvd / zgesvd; forward-promised for
#     rank-revealing decompositions and pseudo-inverse crystals.
#   @arxiv/math/lu_factorization.lapack_realization
#     A = PLU; LAPACK dgetrf / zgetrf; forward-promised for general
#     linear-solve crystals.
#   @arxiv/math/qr_factorization.lapack_realization
#     A = QR; LAPACK dgeqrf / zgeqrf; forward-promised for least-
#     squares crystals.
#   @arxiv/math/spectral_action.chamseddine_connes_numerical
#     S = Tr(f(D/Λ)); the #74 candidate's numerical discharge;
#     forward-promised for the Standard Model empirical crystal
#     via cosmos-mirror's graph-Laplacian engine.
#
# The correspondence's `add_morphism` action (the substrate-decl
# form of the roster expansion) is forward-promised itself; each
# new kind lands via a Bauchladen crystal + a species-shard
# amendment when consumers pull.
#
# === No Rust operational sibling this tick ===
#
# Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] this shard is substrate-decl
# only. The LAPACK dpotrf FFI binding is Reed's next-tick work; the
# empirical crystal for the Cholesky arc lands when that binding
# fires the first `@glue.translate(c_math_silicon, spd_matrix_
# instance)` invocation and the outcome crystallizes in the
# Bauchladen tray.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Cholesky decomposition    Cholesky ~1910; Benoît 1924 (Bull.
#                             Géodésique 2:67-77, posthumous). The
#                             theorem the FIRST morphism_kind
#                             realizes.
#   LAPACK                    Anderson et al. 1992 (`LAPACK Users'
#                             Guide`, SIAM); the reference numerical-
#                             algebra library the discharge targets.
#   BLAS                      Lawson-Hanson-Kincaid-Krogh 1979
#                             (ACM Trans. Math. Softw. 5(3):308-323);
#                             the Level-1 BLAS foundation LAPACK
#                             composes on.
#   Mesland correspondences   Mesland 2013 (arXiv:1304.3802); the
#                             morphism category the @glue family-
#                             root lifts and this species specializes
#                             to math ↔ silicon.
#   KK-theory                 Kasparov 1981 (Math. USSR-Izv. 16(3):
#                             513-572); the underlying KK-cycles
#                             composing via intersection product;
#                             the substrate-altitude form of the
#                             @glue.compose action's non-commutativity.
#   Spectral action           Chamseddine-Connes 1996 (Commun. Math.
#                             Phys. 186:731-750); the numerical
#                             discharge target for the #74 Standard
#                             Model candidate operationalizing at
#                             this species.
#   Numerical linear algebra  Wilkinson 1961 (J. ACM 8:281-330); the
#                             modern floating-point analysis
#                             grounding the restriction's
#                             conditioning bound.
#   Column-major layout       Backus et al. 1957 (FORTRAN 0
#                             specification); the ABI convention
#                             LAPACK's Fortran heritage requires;
#                             the restriction's `layout: column-
#                             major` clause honors this.
#
